Subject: Tonight at 6:30 PM =E2=80=94 Designing Your Future Home & Plans


Join us tonight for Workshop 10 in our Rebuilding 101 series:
Designing Your Future Home & Plans

When: Tuesday, September 23 =C2=B7 6:30 PM
Where: 409 East Woodbury Rd, Altadena, CA 91001
(The NEW Community Resource Center)

This evening=E2=80=99s program highlights how homeowners can move from conc=
ept to
construction with clarity in planning, materials, and design.

=E2=B8=BB

Opening Remarks

We are honored to welcome Chris Holden =E2=80=94 Former State Assembly Majo=
rity
Leader, Pasadena Mayor, and CEO of LA Fire Justice =E2=80=94 to deliver ope=
ning
remarks and set the stage for tonight=E2=80=99s conversation on rebuilding =
with
vision and resilience.

=E2=B8=BB

Featured Guest Speakers

Juliet Chang, AIA =E2=80=94 Architect
Juliet is a licensed architect with deep experience in residential planning
and design. She specializes in helping families navigate the early stages
of rebuilding=E2=80=94developing home layouts that balance lifestyle needs,=
 code
compliance, and long-term value. Juliet integrates sustainable strategies
and modern construction methods to create residences that are beautiful,
functional, and resilient.

Ruben Oganesyan =E2=80=94 Partner, Forma Design
Ruben is a principal at Forma Design, known for crafting residential
interiors and homes that are as practical as they are inspiring. His work
emphasizes planning=E2=80=94aligning architectural vision with construction
realities, budgets, and family needs. At Forma, Ruben helps homeowners
translate design aspirations into buildable, timeless residences rooted in
craft and material quality.

Mo Ahmed =E2=80=94 Founder, Hapi Homes
Mo leads Hapi Homes, a company pioneering the use of light-gauge steel
framing systems and solutions in residential construction. He works
directly with contractors and homeowners to provide structural systems and
housing models that reduce costs, improve durability, and accelerate build
timelines. Mo=E2=80=99s focus is on helping families rebuild smarter with m=
aterials
designed to last.

Freddy Sayegh =E2=80=94 Founder, Alta Design Works
Freddy Sayegh, a former attorney turned design-build strategist, is the
founder of Alta Design Works and co-founder of the Altadena Coalition. He
has guided hundreds of families through post-wildfire recovery by focusing
on residential planning, permitting strategy, and collective negotiation
with architects, contractors, and suppliers. Freddy now dedicates his
expertise to helping communities rebuild efficiently, affordably, and with
long-term resilience.

=E2=B8=BB

What You=E2=80=99ll Learn
=E2=80=A2 How to approach your home=E2=80=99s design concept and layout
=E2=80=A2 The pros and cons of light-gauge steel vs. wood framing in reside=
ntial
builds
=E2=80=A2 How architects, designers, and contractors collaborate on plan se=
ts and
permitting
=E2=80=A2 Budgeting, finishes, and long-term planning for a home that grows=
 with
your family

=E2=B8=BB

Schedule

6:30=E2=80=936:45 PM =C2=B7 Doors open, check-in, refreshments
6:45=E2=80=937:00 PM =C2=B7 Opening Remarks: Chris Holden
7:00=E2=80=938:00 PM =C2=B7 Talks: Chang =E2=80=A2 Oganesyan =E2=80=A2 Ahme=
d =E2=80=A2 Sayegh
8:00=E2=80=938:20 PM =C2=B7 Audience Q&A
8:20=E2=80=938:30 PM =C2=B7 Consults and networking


Moderated By

Freddy Sayegh =E2=80=94 Alta Design Works


Partners: Alta Design Works =E2=80=A2 LA Fire Justice =E2=80=A2 The Altaden=
a Coalition

More info:
http://AltaDesignWorks.com
http://lafirejustice.com

We look forward to seeing you tonight!


*Freddy Sayegh*
